{"id": "DfY6iDNxNO3", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Is Patal Lok really HELL? The Puranas say the 7 worlds below us are more beautiful than heaven itself. 🌏⬇️\n\nBelow the earth lie seven worlds: Atal, Vital, Sutal, Talatal, Mahatal, Rasatal and Patal. The Bhagavata Purana (5.24) calls them \"bila-svarga\", the heavens inside the earth, richer than the heavenly planets. When Narada Muni came back from them, he told the devas they were more delightful than Indra's heaven (Vishnu Purana 2.5).\n\n1. ATAL: Bala, son of Maya, made 96 kinds of magic\n2. VITAL: Shiva lives here as Hatakeshvara, the lord of gold\n3. SUTAL: King Bali's world, where Vishnu himself guards his door, mace in hand\n4. TALATAL: Maya, the demon architect, whose three cities Shiva burned and then gave back\n5. MAHATAL: many-hooded serpents, always afraid of Garuda\n6. RASATAL: demons, enemies of the gods, hiding in holes in fear of Indra\n7. PATAL: Vasuki and the Nagas, where no sun shines and the jewels on their hoods light everything\n\nAnd below all seven, Ananta Shesha holds the whole universe on one of his hoods, like a mustard seed (Bhagavata 5.25.2). The hells (naraka) are a separate place altogether.\n\n📚 Want your kids to grow up knowing these stories? Our picture books bring the gods to life for children. The Navadurga Set is out now. Link in bio · rishikatha.com\n\n💾 Save this, and send it to someone who thinks Patal is hell.\n💬 Which world would YOU visit? Tell us in the comments!\n\n#patallok #patal #sanatandharma #hinduism #bhagavatapurana #vishnupurana #sheshnag #vishnu #mahadev #hindumythology #puranas #vedicwisdom #indianmythology #hindu #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793945026, "like_count": 18055, "comment_count": 51, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1160003596710699a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.756, "asr": 48000, "format_no